{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall place upon it.</b> Upon the screen. Some say it refers back to the word את, which is את פרכת (the screen), like ותצפנו." "<b>And they shall spread a garment entirely of tekhelet.</b> All of it tekhelet." "<b>From above.</b> Some say upon the covering of tahash skin. The correct interpretation in my eyes is that it means 'and they shall spread a garment entirely of tekhelet, from above the screen,' and if for the sake of honor, the first too is possible, and tahash skin because of the body and the dust." "<b>And they shall set its poles.</b> They remove them until the ark is covered. Some say 'they shall set its poles' upon the shoulders of the carriers."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:15.137024501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}